    "Complete list: 22 actions (src/actions.js) and 3 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.js). Both are registered in a single call each (setActionDefinitions, setFeedbackDefinitions). The module README says it is a work in progress and NOT TESTED; the catalog was not tested against a device either.",
    "Third-party module (repository outside the bitfocus organization, hosted on GitHub by a2mSystemes). The manifest repository field points to a different, self-hosted Git server.",
    "Protocol: RossTalk over TCP (config default port 7788, one connection per command or a single connection with the \"TCP Keep Alive\" option), plus TSL UMD v3.1 feedback received over UDP or TCP (config port default 5727). Variables and presets are not catalogued.",
    "Model dependency: the config option \"model\" (solo13 = Carbonite Black Solo 13 with 12 SDI + 1 HDMI, solo = Solo/109 with 6 SDI + 3 HDMI; default solo13) changes the number of inputs. Option lists that depend on it carry a choicesNote instead of a closed list (src/model.js getSources()). Actions and feedbacks are rebuilt on every configUpdated (main.js:24-30).",
    "Text inputs with useVariables are range-checked by the callback, not by Companion: values that are not plain digits or out of range are dropped with a warning in the module log and no command is sent (src/rosstalk.js int()).",
    "xpt: the dropdown field carries a regex (/^[A-Z]+(:[A-Z0-9]+)*$/) in addition to allowCustom; custom values that fail isToken() are dropped with a warning. The Destination list is the buses with a RossTalk destination (src/model.js getBuses()).",
    "The multidropdown fields declare minSelection: 1, which the catalog schema cannot express; an empty selection sends nothing.",
    "Labels are copied as written, including the trailing spaces in \"Transition On/Off Air \" and \"Cut Transition \".",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.12.0: options do not support expressions."
